    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. **finetune/index.js** \u2014 Export constants as named exports\nThe `governance.test.js` test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export. I added named exports for the schema constants at the top of the module.\n\n### 2. **eval/metrics.js** \u2014 Wrap toxicityMetric to handle parameters correctly  \nThe `toxicityMetric` function signature expects `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` was calling all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging all outputs. I wrapped `toxicityMetric` in `DEFAULT_METRICS` to only pass the outputs parameter, allowing it to use the default banned terms list.\n\n**Result:** All 28 tests now pass across 8 test files, including the previously failing governance and eval tests.",
